/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $y'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2$\n\n- $y''+y'=x \\cos x$\n\n- $yy'' - y'+ 9 = 0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6566.json" "file_sha256" "b5a37b22782d16ea63998bb6d506138cf1ce6ed238e9adb8148b0010e5973e9b" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $(y-1)y'.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny''+y'=x \\cos x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x) = 1, b(x) = 1, c(x) = 0,$ and $f(x) = x\\cos{x}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nyy'' - y'+ 9 = 0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $yy''.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6566.json" "file_sha256" "b5a37b22782d16ea63998bb6d506138cf1ce6ed238e9adb8148b0010e5973e9b" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.\n\n- $\\, (2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0$\n\n- $\\,y'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x$\n\n- $\\,y'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6565.json" "file_sha256" "01fc6ca1282d0d81627f87afd6bbbaaa6d0c016235bdd5bb8f6d06e4b634d31c" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0\n$$\n\nis homogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x\n$$\n\nis inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 3e^x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0\n$$\n\nin the form $ay'' + by' + cy = f,$ we have\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y = 8.\n$$\n\nThis equation is inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 8,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6565.json" "file_sha256" "01fc6ca1282d0d81627f87afd6bbbaaa6d0c016235bdd5bb8f6d06e4b634d31c" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the differential equation $2xy'' +y' - y = \\cos x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6568.json" "file_sha256" "04c4eedc6a39f321853110a95ece2adc681295751de61c51b7304a9990aac096" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2xy'' +y' - y = 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6568.json" "file_sha256" "04c4eedc6a39f321853110a95ece2adc681295751de61c51b7304a9990aac096" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x^2y'' + xy' = x+2$\n\n- $9y'' + 4y = e^x, \\quad y(0) = 1,  \\quad  y'(4)= 1$\n\n- $y''+xy'+x^2y= \\sin x, \\quad y(1) = 0,  \\quad  y'(1)= 5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6567.json" "file_sha256" "504d238e2ecf4e89843b168a663f292052855b4eb62c6a949b32041830476a79" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem.**\n\nWith this in mind, let's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- System I is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- System II is not an initial value problem because it consists of a differential equation together with two conditions in *different* locations, $x=0$ and $x=4.$ So this is a **boundary value problem**, not an initial value problem.\n\n- System III is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/example-6567.json" "file_sha256" "504d238e2ecf4e89843b168a663f292052855b4eb62c6a949b32041830476a79" "basis" 1968 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061497/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy=-4x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-4x,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56ce1d7afacf04ffe117aed387b464ff993a9df92116057df1336d797455df06" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "bas