sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "78255a1e4c1f9166f628f62233729cee80ed3ddfc5d9d5d5b049e67fa2ffa056" "basis" 2629 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-93721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x$\n- $\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- ${y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-93721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\frac{1}{x},b(x)=1,c(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=0,c(x)=17,$ and $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-93721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-93721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-93721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-93721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$\n- ${y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0$\n- $x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,c(x)=-1,$ and $f(x)=1.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)={x}^{2},$ and $f(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- $3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $4{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0$\n- $2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0$\n- ${y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,{y}^{′}+{y}^{2}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+{x}^{3}{y}^{′}+2xy=0\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)={x}^{3},c(x)=2x,$ and $f(x)=0.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=x{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=x,c(x)=0,$ and $f(x)=x{e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-130677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $x{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- $5{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+7{y}^{2}=x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n5{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+7{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $7{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.\n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=7,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy=-{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-{x}^{3},$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "homogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-337996" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy=-4x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-4x,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "homogeneous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256