" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338023" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+2y=x$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-6y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y+5x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-(x+2)y=-5x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-5x,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "homogeneous"] ["text" "inhomogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338082" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "inhomogeneous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_A