cted by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+16y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-65016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+16y=0"] ["math" "2{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{′}+8y=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{′}+8y=\\frac{x+1}{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+y=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-65016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+16y=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x,\\,y(-1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=0$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y=8$\n- $x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-3y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem.  It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+2y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-y=5x$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-3x{y}^{′}+4y={x}^{2},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(4)=2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=4$). This is a **boundary value problem.**" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=4x$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-5y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(2)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=3$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-6x{y}^{′}+9y={x}^{2},\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(5)=-2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The second system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=2$).\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=5$). This is a **boundary value problem.**" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-339253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012d