n is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=2$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-339251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-339251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=2,\\,y(5)=2$\n- ${y}^{″}+y={x}^{3}$\n- ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(-3)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-3)=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=5$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-3$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "89e828676ccf83c46fe4cccafe80b303ef8c807dbf04f332771e576ba3cef831"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "q-338533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/state.json" "file_sha256" "9e86ec5c87e6cb4ebe25403fa76a012ddaca79b0a6a8fd49950f6b37e798e127"} {"question" "e-6566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $y'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2$\n\n- $y''+y'=x \\cos x$\n\n- $yy'' - y'+ 9 = 0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6566.json" "file_sha256" "b5a37b22782d16ea63998bb6d506138cf1ce6ed238e9adb8148b0010e5973e9b"} {"question" "e-6566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $(y-1)y'.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny''+y'=x \\cos x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x) = 1, b(x) = 1, c(x) = 0,$ and $f(x) = x\\cos{x}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nyy'' - y'+ 9 = 0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $yy''.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6566.json" "file_sha256" "b5a37b22782d16ea63998bb6d506138cf1ce6ed238e9adb8148b0010e5973e9b"} {"question" "e-6565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.\n\n- $\\, (2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0$\n\n- $\\,y'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x$\n\n- $\\,y'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6565.json" "file_sha256" "01fc6ca1282d0d81627f87afd6bbbaaa6d0c016235bdd5bb8f6d06e4b634d31c"} {"question" "e-6565" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0\n$$\n\nis homogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x\n$$\n\nis inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 3e^x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0\n$$\n\nin the form $ay'' + by' + cy = f,$ we have\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y = 8.\n$$\n\nThis equation is inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 8,$ which is different from zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6565.json" "file_sha256" "01fc6ca1282d0d81627f87afd6bbbaaa6d0c016235bdd5bb8f6d06e4b634d31c"} {"question" "e-6568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the differential equation $2xy'' +y' - y = \\cos x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6568.json" "file_sha256" "04c4eedc6a39f321853110a95ece2adc681295751de61c51b7304a9990aac096"} {"question" "e-6568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2xy'' +y' - y = 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6568.json" "file_sha256" "04c4eedc6a39f321853110a95ece2adc681295751de61c51b7304a9990aac096"} {"question" "e-6567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x^2y'' + xy' = x+2$\n\n- $9y'' + 4y = e^x, \\quad y(0) = 1,  \\quad  y'(4)= 1$\n\n- $y''+xy'+x^2y= \\sin x, \\quad y(1) = 0,  \\quad  y'(1)= 5$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6567.json" "file_sha256" "504d238e2ecf4e89843b168a663f292052855b4eb62c6a949b32041830476a79"} {"question" "e-6567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem.**\n\nWith this in mind, let's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- System I is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- System II is not an initial value problem because it consists of a differential equation together with two conditions in *different* locations, $x=0$ and $x=4.$ So this is a **boundary value problem**, not an initial value problem.\n\n- System III is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14074190/example-6567.json" "file_sha256" "504d238e2ecf4e89843b168a663f292052855b4eb62c6a949b32041830476a79"}] "usage" {"e-6568" [] "q-338004" [] "q-338102" [] "q-339254" [] "e-6565" [] "e-6566" [] "q-337996" [] "q-93721" [] "q-339256" [] "e-6567" [] "q-337990" [] "q-338533" []} "basis" 2884 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186149798 17592186149799 17592186149801 17592186149802 17592186149804 17592186149805 17592186341388 17592186341389 17592186341391 17592186341392 17592186341394 17592186341395 17592186341418 17592186341419 17592186341420 17592186341421 17592186341422 17592186341432 17592186341433 17592186341434 17592186341435 17592186341436 17592186341439 17592186341440 17592186341441 17592186341442 17592186341443 17592186341453 17592186341454 17592186341455 17592186341456 17592186341457 17592186375484 17592186375485 17592186375487 17592186375488 17592186375490 17592186375491 17592186375494 17592186375495 17592186375496 17592186375497 17592186375498] "immutable_fields" [[17592186149797 :answer-field/correct] [17592186149797 :answer-field/id] [17592186149797 :answer-field/key] [17592186149797 :answer-field/type] [17592186149800 :answer-field/correct] [17592186149800 :answer-field/id] [17592186149800 :answer-field/key] [17592186149800 :answer-field/type] [17592186149803 :answer-field/correct] [17592186149803 :answer-field/id] [17592186149803 :answer-field/key] [17592186149803 :answer-field/type] [17592186341387 :answer-field/correct] [17592186341387 :answer-field/id] [17592186341387 :answer-field/key] [17592186341387 :answer-field/type] [17592186341390 :answer-field/correct] [17592186341390 :answer-field/id] [17592186341390 :answer-field/key] [17592186341390 :answer-field/type] [17592186341393 :answer-field/correct] [17592186341393 :answer-field/id] [17592186341393 :answer-field/key] [17592186341393 :answer-field/type] [17592186341417 :answer-field/correct] [1759